{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_27\">Problem 27</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 27\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A large sphere is on a horizontal field on a sunny day. At a certain time the shadow of the sphere reaches out a distance \nof <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m from the point where the sphere touches the ground. At the same instant a meter stick \n(held vertically with one end on the ground) casts a shadow of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> m. What is the radius of the sphere in meters? \n(Assume the sun's rays are parallel and the meter stick is a line segment.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce2f662ea7d2629a671c27cbaee5cec7f39fd934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 9 - 4\\sqrt{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 8\\sqrt{10} - 23\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6-\\sqrt{15}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 10\\sqrt{5}-20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"611\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc279eae862e44052a45fff4ed5a9f929546da4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; import graph;  unitsize(0.5 cm);  pair O = (0,0), T = (0, -2.36067), S = (10, -2.36067), R = (1.05572, 2.11146);   draw(circle(O, 2.3607)); draw(T--S--R--O--cycle); draw(O--S);  label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T, SW); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, W); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, S, SE); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, NE);  [/asy]\" width=\"315\" height=\"148\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the sphere, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the sphere touches the ground, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the tip of the sphere's shadow, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where sun rays that reach the ground near <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> would approach the sphere, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a340678fe76bec6e31d09afc04a968fc936b419d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle RST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> be the angle between the sun's rays and the ground. \n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8fe0bc1f0ab90d60df20bc9e4ccac77d35238e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> must both be tangent to the sphere, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924e1c476b1f47b777660861828a0006d99bf016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS = ST = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe661a8e5848cf6bfb59666ec7d54bb336db9121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8beb8ef068e7cee307ccac72452e57e5ab49076d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle RST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b9a83ed20a8ccfebc6aef3068381328df4e022a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OST = \\frac{\\theta}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Since a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> meter stick casts a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> meter shadow, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7ca7530834a6649b9dc5d2d7797c529ef22f81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fa01a1b72edeec49538875c3d6fa5df590502d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sec \\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+\\tan^2 \\theta}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"331\" height=\"56\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5899dae4f58f197e636b584637d1ca05c83c3597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\cos^2 \\theta} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"258\" height=\"48\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee7dd0c3fabb6fdd1b39ee29532427686f12ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1-\\cos \\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = \\frac{1 - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{5}-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"327\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2575ff0f57129a2d7575dc9bc68b6f0fd914c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = OT = OR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" /> be the radius of the sphere.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a5bc2ac0cd3ea98e1e33a6b89149800b41326f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\frac{r}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"117\" height=\"45\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17afc6dad689d21a9f92b287a9df2df7c47b1d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 10 \\tan\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = 10(\\sqrt{5}-2) = \\boxed{(\\mathbf{E})\\ 10\\sqrt{5} - 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"388\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983